Now Truck import merge and apply. Need edit imports and constructor calls. We need be careful ordering: merge after building everything, after `showExterior(true)` maybe. But merge static parts before attachTrailer (trailer built later attaches and itself merges). Do at end of constructor after showExterior. Also mark dynamic nodes? We'll pass exclude lists per group.

At constructor end:
```
this._optimiseGeometry();
```
Implement:
```
_optimiseGeometry() {
  for (const w of this.wheels) { w.spin.userData.noMerge=true; mergeStaticMeshes(w.spin); }
  this.steeringWheel.userData.noMerge=true; mergeStaticMeshes(this.steeringWheel);
  for (const w of this.wipers) { w.pivot.userData.noMerge=true; mergeStaticMeshes(w.pivot); }
  this.gaugeScreen.userData.noMerge=true; this.navScreen.userData.noMerge=true;
  mergeStaticMeshes(this.cabExterior);
  mergeStaticMeshes(this.mirrors);
  mergeStaticMeshes(this.interior, [this.steeringWheel, this.gaugeScreen, this.navScreen, ...this.wipers.map(w=>w.pivot)]);
  mergeStaticMeshes(this.body, [this.cabExterior, this.mirrors, this.interior]);
}
```
Wait merging `this.body` excludes cabExterior, mirrors, interior; but the chassis rails/crossmembers/fifth wheel/fenders etc are direct children of body and will merge. Good.
Merging `this.interior` with exclude of dynamic nodes; those are descendants, isExcluded checks ancestry starting node until root; if node is inside steering wheel and steering wheel noMerge or in excluded, skip. Good.
Merging `this.cabExterior` includes logo planes (transparent material skipped) and windows transparent skipped. Door logo is transparent maps and depthWrite false → skipped, stays as mesh. fine. Windshield ws transparent skip. Most paint/trim merge.
Merging `this.mirrors` includes mirror glass material not transparent (MeshPhysical metalness .9) so merge.
Wheel spin merge: the tire, rings, 18 treads, hub, cap, 8 bolts. Materials: rubber, rim, chrome → 3 meshes. Good.
Steering wheel merge: leather rim + chromeDark spokes + chrome hub → 3.
Wipers: black + rubber → 2 each.
Gauge/nav screens have transparent? no, MeshBasic opaque; excluded.

Important: `this.showExterior(true)` after merge — visibility on groups preserved. `this.interior` visible false. Fine.

Potential issue: mergeStaticMeshes on body with geometry `.applyMatrix4(relative)` changes normals; okay.
Potential issue: body group's world matrix not updated before merge? merge calls root.updateMatrixWorld(true), which updates children. Good.
But `this.body` contains cabExterior that is not excluded? We pass exclude, yes.

Also the static merged meshes under body are direct children of body; body itself rotates for visual lean. Fine.

Do it.

